; `set` from inside a lambda on a `mut` binding OUTSIDE it. The
; binding is mutable, so the old check passed it - and codegen
; refused it as AX4002, because a closure captures the VALUE it saw
; when its record was built (docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-16): there
; is no cell this store could reach, and the assignment could never
; be observed. MM-MUT-1a; refused in the checker since 2026-08-14.
(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((mut n 0))
    (let ((bump 
      (lambda (k)
        {
          (set n (+ n k))
          n
        }
      )
    ))
      {
        (bump 5)
        n
      }
    )
  )
)
